... (translate remaining stanzas likewise, keeping <p class="poem"> and <br> tags unchanged).</p>","translation_quote":"(Entire hymn stanzas left in English inside multiple <p class="poem"> elements) "},{"location":"source.title and translation.title","severity":"major","source_quote":"Abide With Me, Fast Falls The Eventide","suggested_fix":"Translate the article title into Spanish in the title field, using idiomatic, internationally intelligible language while preserving meaning. Example: "Quédate conmigo: cae veloz el crepúsculo" (or a close idiomatic rendering). Do not alter HTML tags or attributes—replace only the title string.","translation_quote":"Abide With Me, Fast Falls The Eventide"},{"location":"source.html — hymn reference within body (sentence about origin of hymn)","severity":"major","source_quote":"Se dice que fue su encuentro con Dios al lado de ese hombre moribundo lo que impulsó el noble himno de Lyte, «Jesus, I My Cross Have Taken».","suggested_fix":"Translate the quoted hymn title into Spanish as part of the running text. Quoted substantive prose (including hymn titles used as quoted lines) must be rendered into the target language. For example: «Jesús, yo he tomado mi cruz» (placed within the existing quotation marks). Preserve surrounding punctuation and HTML structure.","translation_quote":"«Jesus, I My Cross Have Taken» left in English in the translation."}],"passed":false,"score":70}
